msgstr ""

msgid "Contact forms, stored entries and floating contact actions."
msgstr ""

msgid "The theme includes a Form block and floating contact buttons. A separate visual form builder is planned; the existing Form block remains available."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this for enquiries and quick phone or messaging actions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Insert a Form block and configure fields and destinations."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configure floating contact channels in the Customizer."
msgstr ""

msgid "Submit a test entry and verify delivery and stored entries."
msgstr ""

msgid "Email delivery also depends on hosting and mail configuration. Do not assume a visible success message proves delivery to the inbox."
msgstr ""

msgid "SEO and reading tools"
msgstr ""

msgid "Headings, contents, sharing and SEO plugin compatibility."
msgstr ""

msgid "Theme presentation supports readable content and integrates with Rank Math or Yoast metadata through AI Designer. A dedicated SEO plugin is still recommended for broader SEO management."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this when preparing pages for visitors and search engines."
msgstr ""

msgid "Write a logical heading structure and descriptive image alt text."
msgstr ""

msgid "Configure blog reading tools and sharing where relevant."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review SEO metadata, indexing and sitemap in your SEO plugin."
msgstr ""

msgid "Markup checks do not replace a visual or search-console audit. Avoid duplicate SEO plugins."
msgstr ""

msgid "Per-block CSS, local fonts and performance options."
msgstr ""

msgid "Only the required block CSS is loaded and generated styles are cached. Local font delivery avoids a separate font request to an external service."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this before and after adding large media or third-party plugins."
msgstr ""

msgid "Resize images to their displayed purpose."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review performance settings and use one appropriate caching plugin."
msgstr ""

msgid "Measure representative pages on mobile after clearing relevant caches."
msgstr ""

msgid "Large videos, excessive plugins and third-party scripts still affect speed. Clear caches after a visible style change before diagnosing it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Import, export and backups"
msgstr ""

msgid "Transfer theme configuration between sites."
msgstr ""

msgid "Studio can export and import theme settings. This configuration file is not a backup of posts, media, products or the database."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this for repeatable client setups or before major configuration changes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Export the current settings and keep a separate full-site backup."
msgstr ""

msgid "Import only a trusted theme configuration file."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review menus, media IDs and page references on the destination site."
msgstr ""

msgid "Imports can replace current settings. Site-specific image and page IDs may need reassignment."
msgstr ""

msgid "What is built in?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Reduce overlapping plugins and keep the stack focused."
msgstr ""

msgid "Header/footer layouts, blocks, forms, floating contact buttons, sharing and reading tools are included. WooCommerce supplies commerce; SEO and caching plugins can complement the theme."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this when choosing which plugins a new site really needs."
msgstr ""

msgid "List the functions your site needs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check the built-in guides before installing another plugin."
msgstr ""

msgid "Test any plugin removal on a draft site and keep backups."
msgstr ""

msgid "Do not disable a plugin merely because its name resembles a built-in feature. Existing content may still depend on it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Theme FAQ and updates"
msgstr ""

msgid "Resolve missing menus, stale styles and update notices."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use a child theme for file changes. GitHub Releases supply update ZIPs; saved settings and content remain when WordPress replaces theme files."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this when an update or a recent design change does not appear."
msgstr ""

msgid "Confirm the installed version in Appearance → Themes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use Check for updates above to refresh the GitHub cache."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the check fails, verify hosting access to GitHub and try again later."
msgstr ""

msgid "Versions before 1.73.3 keep their own cache even when WordPress Check again is used. This cannot be repaired remotely by publishing a new ZIP alone."
msgstr ""

msgid "Connect, choose a model and set budgets"
msgstr ""

msgid "Connect the API before starting paid work."
msgstr ""

msgid "Store your API key in Settings, verify the connection and choose a text model and optional image model. The key stays on the server."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this on first setup or when a provider/model is unavailable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Open Settings and connect your API key yourself."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose a model, then set task and daily budgets."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check the reported balance before requesting images or long tasks."
msgstr ""

msgid "Costs vary by model, number of steps and image size. A short text task usually needs fewer calls than a full page with images; no fixed price is guaranteed. A zero budget disables that limit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Explain which model and budget suit one draft service page before starting."
msgstr ""

msgid "Estimate the steps for a homepage with three images and wait for my approval."
msgstr ""

msgid "Guidelines and a clear brief"
msgstr ""

msgid "Give the agent facts, brand rules and content constraints."
msgstr ""

msgid "Guidelines supply reusable brand context. Include audience, real services, tone, contact details, colors, prohibited claims and image preferences; distinguish facts from ideas."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this before several tasks for the same business."
msgstr ""

msgid "Write concise factual Guidelines."
msgstr ""

msgid "Give a page goal, audience and measurable outcome in each task."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ask the agent to identify missing facts before writing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Weak: “Make it beautiful.” Better: specify the business, visitor, page, desired action, style and constraints. Never invent testimonials, prices or certifications."
msgstr ""

msgid "For our laundry service in Bac Ninh, propose a homepage for local households. Ask about missing facts before drafting."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read our Guidelines and flag any facts you need before writing a landing page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Discuss first, build second"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use one task per clear goal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Agree on page structure, palette, typography and image direction before building drafts. BIGSPY blocks remain editable by hand after AI work."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this for a new site or a redesign with several decisions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Connect the API and choose a model/budget."
msgstr ""

msgid "Fill Guidelines and describe one concrete goal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Approve a plan, let the agent draft, then review desktop and mobile."
msgstr ""

msgid "High effort allows more steps; it does not guarantee a particular design. Keep Workspace open while a task runs and review actual results."
msgstr ""

msgid "Discuss a five-section service page with me. Show the outline and palette, then wait before building."
msgstr ""

msgid "Compare two visual directions for this page; do not change the site yet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Design pages with editable blocks"
msgstr ""

msgid "Homepages, landing pages and service pages."
msgstr ""

msgid "The agent creates layouts with the theme’s registered blocks and patterns rather than an unstructured code dump. You can continue editing in the WordPress block editor."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this when creating a draft page from an agreed brief."
msgstr ""

msgid "Define the audience, goal, sections and real business facts."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ask for a draft and preview it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Check mobile width, H1, links, images and copy before publishing approval."
msgstr ""

msgid "AI markup checks are useful hints, not a full browser audit. Use theme controls to refine spacing and responsive behavior manually."
msgstr ""

msgid "Build an unpublished service page from the outline we agreed. Use editable BIGSPY blocks and check its heading structure."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create a draft landing page focused on requesting a quote, with a clear mobile call to action."
msgstr ""

msgid "Images and image SEO"
msgstr ""

msgid "ImageGen, optimization and image metadata."
msgstr ""

msgid "Generate images for a defined purpose, optimize supported media and fill descriptive alt text. Image generation can charge the API even when later task changes are undone."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this for authentic-looking illustrations when suitable owned images are unavailable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Specify subject, style, aspect ratio and placement."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review the estimated scope and approve any required image request."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review the generated image, file size and alt text before using it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Generated media remains in Media Library after undo. Image optimization may change bytes that snapshots cannot restore. Never claim a generated person is a real customer."
msgstr ""

msgid "Propose one hero image for this service page, including aspect ratio and prompt. Wait before generating."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review this page’s image sizes and suggest descriptive alt text without changing the originals yet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Write new articles"
msgstr ""

msgid "Create drafts from topics, keywords and verified facts."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ask for an outline first, then a readable draft for a specific audience. Supply references and distinguish editorial ideas from claims needing verification."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this for a new educational or business blog post."
msgstr ""

msgid "Provide a topic, search intent and factual sources."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review the outline before requesting the full draft."
msgstr ""

msgid "Edit facts, links and metadata before publishing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Avoid keyword stuffing and invented statistics. The agent does not replace an expert review for high-stakes subjects."
msgstr ""

msgid "Propose an outline for a post explaining how to prepare clothes for a laundry pickup service."
msgstr ""

msgid "Write an unpublished article from this approved outline using only the facts in our Guidelines."
msgstr ""

msgid "Improve existing articles and SEO"
msgstr ""

msgid "Review headings, intent, copy and supported SEO metadata."
msgstr ""

msgid "The agent can inspect existing content and propose improvements, including Rank Math or Yoast metadata. Changes to published content require approval."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this for an existing page with unclear structure or outdated copy."
msgstr ""

msgid "Identify the exact post/page and target audience."
msgstr ""

msgid "Request an audit and a proposed edit list."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review the approval card and verify the final content."
msgstr ""

msgid "Search ranking is not guaranteed. A correct heading hierarchy and metadata are only part of SEO."
msgstr ""

msgid "Audit this published article’s headings and search intent. List changes before editing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Suggest an SEO title and description for this page; keep the current page body unchanged."
msgstr ""

msgid "Product descriptions"
msgstr ""

msgid "Draft and refine WooCommerce product copy."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use verified product specifications, benefits and usage details to improve descriptions. The agent does not process orders, customer data or payments."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this when adding products or improving an existing catalog."
msgstr ""

msgid "Provide accurate specifications and the product ID."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review draft copy and unsupported claims."
msgstr ""

msgid "Approve updates and test the product page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Do not invent availability, discounts, warranties or certifications. Validate variations and prices manually."
msgstr ""

msgid "Draft a product description using these specifications; mark missing details as questions."
msgstr ""

msgid "Improve this product’s benefits and readability without changing its price or variations."
msgstr ""

msgid "Menus, footer and brand settings"
msgstr ""

msgid "Coordinate reusable layout and site-wide design changes."
msgstr ""

msgid "The agent can work with menus, reusable UX Blocks, supported header/footer options, logo, colors and typography. Live and global changes use approval cards."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this when applying an agreed brand consistently across the site."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ask the agent to inspect current menus and design options first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create reusable content as drafts and preview it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Approve publishing and assignment separately where required."
msgstr ""

msgid "A menu must be assigned to a location and its Menu element must exist in the active header. A footer source must be published and public."
msgstr ""

msgid "Inspect our header and menu assignments, then explain why navigation is missing on mobile."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create a draft reusable footer from our verified contact details. Wait before publishing or assigning it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Advice-only tasks"
msgstr ""

msgid "Analyze and plan without AI writes to the site."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose Advice only before creating a task. The server blocks AI write tools in this mode, while the agent can inspect allowed site information and produce a manual checklist."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this for audits, comparisons and planning."
msgstr ""

msgid "Select Advice only in Workspace."
msgstr ""

msgid "Create a new task and define what to inspect."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review the findings and complete the manual checklist yourself."
msgstr ""

msgid "The task mode is server-enforced. Start a separate Design task if you later want implementation."
msgstr ""

msgid "In advice-only mode, audit our homepage and return a prioritized manual checklist."
msgstr ""

msgid "Compare our current footer with our Guidelines and list improvements without changing anything."
msgstr ""

msgid "Permissions and approval cards"
msgstr ""

msgid "Three permission levels enforced on the server."
msgstr ""

msgid "Level 1 covers permitted reads and drafts. Level 2 requires a human approval for live/global changes and other sensitive tools. Level 3 is guidance only for prohibited actions such as accounts, security, updates, plugin deletion and payments."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this whenever an approval card appears or a task proposes global changes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Review the exact scope, before/after values, cost and undo limits."
msgstr ""

msgid "Choose Agree, do it yourself, or Skip."
msgstr ""

msgid "Verify the result before approving another change."
msgstr ""

msgid "Model text cannot approve itself. Plugin installation, where supported, requires explicit approval; plugin updates and deletion remain outside the agent’s tools."
msgstr ""

msgid "Explain the exact changes and undo limits before requesting any live-site approval."
msgstr ""

msgid "Prepare a manual checklist for actions your tools are not allowed to perform."
msgstr ""

msgid "Undo, costs and troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

msgid "Understand what a task snapshot can restore."
msgstr ""

msgid "Task undo restores supported content and configuration snapshots. API charges and generated media remain; plugin files/data remain after deactivation; optimized image bytes may not be restorable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use this before a large task, after a failure or when reviewing costs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Keep a full-site backup and use one clear task per goal."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stop a running task before undoing it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read the log, check restored content and review provider charges separately."
msgstr ""

msgid "A disconnected API, exhausted budget or unavailable model can pause work. Reconnect, review the budget or choose an available model; never increase the budget without understanding the cost."
msgstr ""

msgid "Summarize this task’s changes, API cost and what undo would leave behind."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read the latest task error and suggest the smallest safe next step without increasing the budget."
msgstr ""

